  "Hemagglutinin binds sialic acid residues on the surface of respiratory epithelial cells, mediating viral attachment and subsequent fusion and entry. Antibodies against hemagglutinin are the main target of protective immunity and the basis for most vaccine formulations, which is why antigenic changes in hemagglutinin drive the need for updated vaccines.",
