  difficulty="medium",
  why={"Transmission occurs efficiently and sustainably from person": "Current avian influenza strains have not achieved efficient sustained human-to-human transmission, which is the pattern this vignette illustrates.",
       "Transmission requires a mosquito vector present on the farm": "Avian influenza spreads through respiratory secretions and contact with infected birds, not by an insect vector.",
       "Transmission is prevented entirely by existing seasonal influenza": "Seasonal vaccines target circulating human strains and do not reliably protect against a distinct avian subtype.",
       "Transmission occurs equally well through casual, non-occupational": "The pattern described, illness in exposed workers but not unexposed family, argues against equally efficient casual transmission."},
