  difficulty="medium",
  why={"Bronchospasm from IgE-mediated mast cell degranulation": "This mechanism describes an allergic or asthmatic process, not the epithelial necrosis and mucus plugging typical of RSV bronchiolitis.",
       "Fibrous scarring of the bronchioles from chronic inflammatory": "Fibrous scarring reflects a chronic process, not the acute infectious injury of RSV bronchiolitis.",
       "Eosinophilic infiltration identical to that seen in allergic": "RSV bronchiolitis is characterized by neutrophilic and lymphocytic inflammation with epithelial necrosis, not an eosinophil-predominant allergic pattern.",
       "Vascular congestion of the bronchial mucosa without epithelial": "RSV causes direct epithelial necrosis, not simply vascular congestion with intact epithelium."},
